    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1321" root="انث" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِئْنَاثٌ</span></b>  A woman <i>who usually brings forth females:</i> (S, M, K:) and a man <i>who usually begets
female children;</i> for the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِفْعَالٌ</span> applies
equally to both sexes: (S:) the contr. epithet is
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِذْكَارٌ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤَنَّثٌ</span>, in two places.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ مِئْنَاثٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنِيثٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَيْفٌ مِئْنَاثٌ</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِئْنَاثَةٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنِيثٌ</span>.

